//! task: write
//! ask: Return the quotient and remainder of a divided by b as two functions.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.4, §8.6
//! explain: `/` on two integers is the truncated quotient and traps on a zero divisor; `residuum` is the remainder. Both operands must have the same type. There is no `%` token: remainder is the contextual word `residuum`.

publica functio quotiens(a: u32, b: u32) -> u32 {
    redde a / b;
}

publica functio reliquum(a: u32, b: u32) -> u32 {
    redde a residuum b;
}
